-- 141_playable_loop.surql -- THE PLAYABLE LOOP: a human drives the real MvC2 frame function.
-- SUPERGUN ENGINE lane, 2026-09-04 (odd seeds). Doc: mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/RECEIPT-RUNNER-PLAY.md
-- Idempotent and replayable; explicit edge ids; additive fields only on findings owned by earlier seeds.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:tool_play_session SET kind='tool', strength='code',
  ref='mvc-live-skins-quarters/d3dcap/receipt/play_session.py + d3dcap/receipt/runner/rr_runner.cpp --play --play-frames',
  note='Chains four stages, three already gated: dcram_build.py builds DC-RAM from the user own arc with no memory dump (GATE 3/4); rr_runner --play reads XInput (dynamically loaded, with a keyboard fallback), maps it to the two seat words and ticks FUN_140118950 paced at 60 Hz (NEW); --harvest-dump plus rr-tape turn the per-tick memory into a v5 tape (GATE 2); player.html renders the tape (L1/L3, in production). rr_runner prints NO INPUT WAS EVER PRESSED when the pad stayed at zero, so a mechanically green run can never be mistaken for a human-in-the-loop result.';

UPSERT finding:playable_loop_chain_closes SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-04',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The playable chain closes end to end at 60 Hz; the human half is NOT yet proven',
  statement='Measured on a 120-frame session over the arc-built stage-9 anchor with --harvest-dump on and nobody at the controls: 120 frames in 2,005 ms = 59.8 fps sustained. Tick alone (FUN_140118950) p50 0.176 ms, p90 0.266, p99 0.421, max 0.541. Per-frame WORK (pad read + tick + harvest dump), excluding the 60 Hz sleep: p50 8.96 ms, p99 12.26, max 12.30. Harvest plus rr-tape for the whole session 0.2 s, producing a 121-frame 70,785 B tape. emit_seq on that tape renders 35,380 draws over 60 frames (73.4 MB seq), so a PLAY-PRODUCED tape goes through the gated render pipeline. WHERE THE FRAME GOES: the tick is about 1 percent of the 16.667 ms budget and the per-tick state capture is about 54 percent -- the dominant cost is the 32 MB memcmp that --harvest-dump uses to find changed DC-RAM pages, which is a capture concern, not an engine one.',
  caveat='NO HUMAN HAS PRESSED A BUTTON YET. All numbers above were taken with the pad at zero. Also: the render is NOT live -- the player currently plays blind with pad word and px/py printed per frame, and pixels are produced from the tape after the session.';

UPSERT finding:play_pad_word_is_the_whole_input SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-04',
  title='A human pressing a button produces the identical object a receipt replays',
  statement='FUN_140118950 takes the two seat words as its entire input (DETERMINISM-CONTRACT s1), so there is no second input path that could be wrong: the pad word a gamepad synthesises IS the seat word a tape records. Bit layout, pre-existing and verified in docs/CONFIRMED-TAPE-AND-FLYR-REPLAY.md s5: 0x10 UP, 0x20 RIGHT, 0x40 DOWN, 0x80 LEFT, 0x200 A1, 0x800 A2, 0x1000 HP, 0x2000 HK, 0x4000 LK, 0x8000 LP. Re-checked against recorded tapes before use: 0x000080 walk left, 0x000020 walk right, 0x0020C0 down-left plus HK. Gamepad mapping X=LP Y=HP A=LK B=HK LB=A1 RB=A2 with d-pad or left stick for directions; keyboard fallback arrows plus Z/X/C and A/S/D.';

UPSERT finding:play_py_is_not_evidence_of_a_human SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-04',
  title='The idle animation moves py on its own, so py cannot evidence a human input',
  statement='A first version of the play loop declared FIRST MOVE on frame 1 with pad 000000, because it compared both px and py against their start values and py oscillates by itself while the character idles (observed swinging between about -12.9 and +12.9 with no input at all). px is stable at rest. rr_runner now reports two separate things: the first frame with a NON-ZERO pad, and the first px change AFTER one. This is the same family of mistake as treating node+0xE8 as a DC-RAM pointer: a signal that looks like the thing you want but is generated by the system itself.';

RELATE finding:playable_loop_chain_closes->cites:play_chain_tool->source:tool_play_session;
RELATE finding:play_pad_word_is_the_whole_input->cites:play_pad_tool->source:tool_play_session;
RELATE finding:play_py_is_not_evidence_of_a_human->cites:play_py_tool->source:tool_play_session;
